File: crate-jmap-chat-server/src/message.rs

In the augmented patch block (around line 451), after the existing editedAt and deletedAt injection logic, add:

    // Spec: when readAt is set without readDisposition, default to "displayed".
    if let Some(obj) = augmented.as_object_mut() {
        if obj.contains_key("readAt") && !obj.contains_key("readDisposition") {
            obj.insert("readDisposition".to_owned(), json!("displayed"));
        }
    }

readDisposition is NOT added to MESSAGE_READONLY — it is client-settable per spec. Any value (including extension values) passes through to the backend unchanged; the server only supplies the default.

No other changes to the handler. The backend stores whatever readDisposition arrives in the patch, same as all other non-server-set fields.
